<title>NORWAY: TABLE-SAS H1 PRE-TAX PROFIT FALLS 6 PCT.</title>
<headline>TABLE-SAS H1 PRE-TAX PROFIT FALLS 6 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30.</p>
<p>				(millions of Swedish crowns)</p>
<p>  Group pre-tax result	 1,106   vs	 1,178</p>
<p>  Operating revenue	   18,989   vs	17,442</p>
<p>Operating result before</p>
<p>		    writeoffs    1,936   vs	 1,975</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of carrier is Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS), which is owned jointly by the governments of Sweden, Norway and Denmark and private investors.</p>
<p>A Reuters poll of seven analysts forecast an average pre-tax profit of 594 million Swedish crowns for the first six months 1997.  </p>
<p>  Group pre-tax result	 1,106   vs	 1,178</p>
<p>  Operating expenses	  17,053   vs	15,467</p>
<p>  Depreciation	  minus    913   vs  minus  893</p>
<p>Result before financial</p>
<p>			   items   1,135   vs	 1,206</p>
<p>  Financial items	  minus  44   vs  minus   28</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
